Package: jellyfin-videotools
Version: 12.4.1
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ffmpeg, adduser, libicu72 | libicu71 | libicu70, libssl3 | libssl1.1
Recommends: vainfo
Maintainer: Dimerry <dimerry@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Dimerry/jellyfin-videotools
Description: Jellyfin media server fork with video transcode and cut tools
 A self-contained build of the Jellyfin 12.4 fork that adds:
  * transcode a video to H.265 or AV1 from the context menu, picking Intel QSV,
    NVIDIA NVENC or software encoding automatically,
  * cut a clip (trim start/end, rotate) with stream copy,
  * a background job queue with progress, retry and cancel,
  * sorting by bitrate and file size, image rotation, and an /emby
    compatibility layer for tools written against the Emby API.
 .
 The .NET runtime is bundled, so no .NET installation is required. ffmpeg is
 used from the system package.
